IMPORT prelude

-- Control of Manufacture Act 1959 (Singapore) -- who must register to manufacture which goods (ss 2, 3, First and Second Schedules),
-- the Minister's exemption (s 14(1)), registration, conditions and the protection for existing manufacturers (s 5), revocation and its
-- deadlines (s 6), the Registrar's demands for information (s 7), offences, fines and composition (ss 8, 9, 14(3)) and liability for
-- a servant (s 11).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CMA1959.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021" and each page is marked "Informal Consolidation -- version in force
-- from 9/3/2025". The latest amendment annotated is Act 5 of 2025 (Electronic Gazette and Legislation Act 2025) wef 9 March 2025, in
-- s 4(2), (3). The First Schedule carries S 630/2003, S 453/2004 and S 553/2016.
--
-- SECTION NUMBERS. The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body by one (it numbers "Short title"
-- as 2). This file follows the body: s 1 short title, s 2 interpretation, s 3 the prohibition, s 4 the Registrar, s 5 registration,
-- and so on to s 17.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0097 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short, so nearly all of it that bears on a manufacturer is encoded. Not encoded: the appointment of the
-- Registrar (s 4), powers of entry and inspection (s 10), the annual duty (s 12 -- no order was retrieved, so no rate is known),
-- variation of the First Schedule (s 13), the Minister's production cap beyond its deemed-condition effect (s 14(2), (3)),
-- compliance with other written law (s 15), rules (s 16) and their presentation to Parliament (s 17). No rules, orders or forms made
-- under the Act were retrieved, so the prescribed form, information and fee (s 5(1), (5)) are not known.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Control of Manufacture Act 1959 -- registration`

DECLARE Goods IS ONE OF
    `beer or stout`
    `cigars`
    `drawn steel products`
    `chewing gum`
    `oral dental gum that is a health product`
    `cigarettes`
    `matches`
    `wine`
    `furniture`

DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `making the goods or a part of them`
    `altering, finishing, cleaning, assembling or processing the goods`
    `adapting the goods for sale`
    `buying and reselling the goods unchanged`

§§ `First and Second Schedules -- specified goods`

-- First Schedule: "1. Beer and stout 2. Cigars 3. Drawn steel products 4. Chewing gum, bubble gum, dental chewing gum or any like
-- substance, not being a health product categorised as an oral dental gum or a therapeutic product in the First Schedule to the Health
-- Products Act 2007."
-- Second Schedule: "1. Cigarettes 2. Matches".
-- Wine and furniture are in neither Schedule; they are here to show what falls outside.
GIVEN `the goods` IS A Goods
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods are in the First Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the goods`
    WHEN `beer or stout` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cigars` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `drawn steel products` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `chewing gum` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the goods` IS A Goods
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods are in the Second Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the goods`
    WHEN `cigarettes` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `matches` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 2: "'goods' includes all materials, commodities and articles for the time being specified in the First or Second Schedule".
-- "Includes" is read here as confining the Act to the scheduled goods, since s 8(1) penalises only manufacture of "goods specified in
-- the First or Second Schedule". That reading is an inference.
GIVEN `the goods` IS A Goods
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods are specified goods` IF
    `the goods are in the First Schedule` `the goods` OR `the goods are in the Second Schedule` `the goods`

§§ `2 -- manufacture`

-- s 2: "'manufacture' means -- (a) the making of any goods or part of any goods; (b) the altering, ornamenting, finishing, cleaning or
-- washing or the breaking up or the assembling or processing in any form of any goods; or (c) the adapting for sale of any goods, in
-- which machinery operated by mechanical power is used".
-- The deposit sets "in which machinery operated by mechanical power is used" on the line after (c), within it. This file reads the
-- power-machinery condition as qualifying (c) only. That is an inference from the layout: it may instead qualify all three limbs.
GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity, `powered machinery is used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is manufacture` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `making the goods or a part of them` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `altering, finishing, cleaning, assembling or processing the goods` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `adapting the goods for sale` THEN `powered machinery is used`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3 and 14(1) -- registration required`

-- s 3: "no person shall engage in the manufacture for sale or other commercial purpose of any goods unless he is registered under the
-- provisions of this Act in respect of that manufacture."
-- s 14(1): "The Minister may exempt any person from any or all of the provisions of this Act."
GIVEN `the goods` IS A Goods, `the activity` IS AN Activity, `powered machinery is used` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `for sale or other commercial purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `registration is required` IF
        `the goods are specified goods` `the goods`
    AND `the activity is manufacture` `the activity` `powered machinery is used`
    AND `for sale or other commercial purpose`
    AND (NOT `exempted by the Minister`)

-- s 8(1): "Any person who engages in the manufacture for sale or other commercial purposes of any goods specified in the First or Second
-- Schedule without being registered under this Act in respect of those goods shall be guilty of an offence".
GIVEN `the goods` IS A Goods, `the activity` IS AN Activity, `powered machinery is used` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `for sale or other commercial purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN, `registered for those goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `manufacturing unregistered is an offence` IF
        `registration is required` `the goods` `the activity` `powered machinery is used` `for sale or other commercial purpose` `exempted by the Minister`
    AND (NOT `registered for those goods`)

§§ `5 -- registration, conditions and existing manufacturers`

-- s 5(2): "The Registrar may in his discretion register or refuse to register any person ... and at the time of registering any person
-- may impose such conditions as he thinks fit."
-- s 5(3): where a person satisfies the Minister that immediately before the specification of the goods "in the First Schedule" he
-- (a) "was engaged in the manufacture in Singapore of those goods"; or (b) "had bona fide made substantial preparations for, or incurred
-- expense with a view to," that manufacture, "an application by that person for registration in respect of those goods ... within 6
-- months of the specification shall not be refused, and no condition may be imposed in respect thereof."
-- The protection names the First Schedule only. A cigarette or match maker (Second Schedule) gets none. "Within 6 months" is taken as
-- at most 6 whole months; the encoding counts months as a number and does not compute calendar dates.
GIVEN `the goods` IS A Goods, `was manufacturing them in Singapore before specification` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had made substantial preparations before specification` IS A BOOLEAN, `months from specification to application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is protected` IF
        `the goods are in the First Schedule` `the goods`
    AND (`was manufacturing them in Singapore before specification` OR `had made substantial preparations before specification`)
    AND `months from specification to application` AT MOST 6

-- s 5(2), (3): a protected application must be granted, unconditionally; any other may be refused or granted on conditions.
GIVEN `the application is protected now` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may refuse or impose conditions` IF
    NOT `the application is protected now`

-- s 5(6): "Registration shall not be transferable from one person to another without the written consent of the Minister, which consent
-- shall not be withheld in respect of any registration to which subsection (3) applies."
GIVEN `the Minister consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registration may be transferred` IF
    `the Minister consented in writing`

GIVEN `the registration was protected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister must consent to a transfer` IF
    `the registration was protected`

§§ `5(4), 6(3) -- appeals`

-- s 5(4): a person aggrieved by a condition or a refusal "may appeal in writing to the Minister whose decision shall be final."
-- s 6(3): a person aggrieved by a revocation "may within 14 days of the notification to him of the grounds of the decision appeal to the
-- General Division of the High Court whose decision shall be final."
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `a refusal to register`
    `a condition of registration`
    `a revocation`

DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `the Minister`
    `the General Division of the High Court`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A Forum
`the appeal lies to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a revocation` THEN `the General Division of the High Court`
    OTHERWISE `the Minister`

§§ `6 -- revocation`

-- s 6(1): the Registrar may, "after notice to the registered manufacturer and after such inquiry as he thinks fit", revoke where (a) the
-- registration "was effected as a result of a misrepresentation of facts"; (b) "any condition of registration has been contravened";
-- or (c) the manufacturer "has for a continuous period of not less than 3 months ceased to manufacture" the goods.
-- s 6(5), (6): the Registrar may by notice require a minimum quantity; one who fails to comply "shall be deemed to have ceased to
-- manufacture those goods."
-- s 14(3): one who fails to comply with a production cap under s 14(2) "shall ... be deemed to have contravened a condition of
-- registration."
GIVEN `months of continuous stoppage` IS A NUMBER, `failed a minimum-quantity notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the manufacturer has ceased to manufacture` IF
    `months of continuous stoppage` AT LEAST 3 OR `failed a minimum-quantity notice`

GIVEN `breached a condition` IS A BOOLEAN, `exceeded a production cap` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a condition is contravened` IF
    `breached a condition` OR `exceeded a production cap`

GIVEN `registered by misrepresentation` IS A BOOLEAN, `breached a condition` IS A BOOLEAN, `exceeded a production cap` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months of continuous stoppage` IS A NUMBER, `failed a minimum-quantity notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may revoke` IF
        `notice was given`
    AND (    `registered by misrepresentation`
         OR  `a condition is contravened` `breached a condition` `exceeded a production cap`
         OR  `the manufacturer has ceased to manufacture` `months of continuous stoppage` `failed a minimum-quantity notice`)

-- s 6(2): the Registrar "shall within 7 days of revoking any registration inform the registered manufacturer in writing of the revocation
-- and the grounds" and of the right of appeal.
-- s 6(3): appeal "within 14 days of the notification to him of the grounds".
-- s 6(4): revocation "shall take effect 21 days after the making of the decision ... or, in the event of an appeal ... on the
-- determination of the appeal."
-- Days are counted as day numbers; no calendar or public-holiday rule is applied.
GIVEN `day of the decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day to notify the manufacturer` MEANS
    `day of the decision` PLUS 7

GIVEN `day notified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day to appeal` MEANS
    `day notified` PLUS 14

GIVEN `day of the decision` IS A NUMBER, `an appeal was brought` IS A BOOLEAN, `day the appeal is determined` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day the revocation takes effect` MEANS
    IF `an appeal was brought` THEN `day the appeal is determined` ELSE `day of the decision` PLUS 21

§§ `7 -- returns and information`

-- s 7(1): the Registrar may by notice call for "such information pertaining to the conditions of his registration as the Registrar may
-- require". (2): nothing authorises the Registrar "to require a registered manufacturer to disclose any secret process".
-- (3): the information is confidential and "shall not be used, published or disclosed otherwise than for the purposes of this Act
-- without the consent in writing of the registered manufacturer."
GIVEN `pertains to the conditions of registration` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a secret process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may require the information` IF
    `pertains to the conditions of registration` AND (NOT `is a secret process`)

GIVEN `for the purposes of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `manufacturer consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the information may be disclosed` IF
    `for the purposes of this Act` OR `manufacturer consented in writing`

§§ `8, 9 -- offences, fines and composition`

-- s 8(1): unregistered manufacture -- "a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- exceeding $1,000 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction."
-- s 8(2): failing to comply with a condition -- "a fine not exceeding $10,000" and a further $1,000 a day after conviction.
-- s 14(3): exceeding a production cap is a deemed contravention of a condition, so s 8(2) applies (an inference: s 14(3) says "for the
-- purposes of this Act").
-- s 8(3): omitting or refusing to supply information under s 7, or supplying information known or believed false -- "a fine not
-- exceeding $1,000". No further daily fine.
-- No offence in the Act carries imprisonment.
-- s 9: the Registrar may compound "any offence under this Act by collecting ... a sum of money not exceeding $1,000."
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `manufacturing unregistered`
    `breaching a condition`
    `exceeding a production cap`
    `failing to supply information`
    `supplying false information`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `manufacturing unregistered` THEN 50000 PLUS 1000 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`
    WHEN `breaching a condition` THEN 10000 PLUS 1000 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`
    WHEN `exceeding a production cap` THEN 10000 PLUS 1000 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`
    OTHERWISE 1000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    1000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence carries imprisonment` IF
    FALSE

§§ `11 -- liability for an agent or servant`

-- s 11: a person liable to a penalty for any act or default "shall be liable to the same penalty for every similar act ... of any agent
-- or servant employed by him in connection with the manufacture of the goods or class of goods in respect of which he is registered".
-- Read literally, the extension reaches only goods the employer is registered for. An unregistered maker's servant is not within s 11;
-- the unregistered maker is in any case himself the one who "engages in the manufacture" under s 8(1). That second point is an inference.
GIVEN `the employer is liable for a similar own act` IS A BOOLEAN, `the servant was employed in that manufacture` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the employer is registered for those goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is liable for the servant's act` IF
        `the employer is liable for a similar own act`
    AND `the servant was employed in that manufacture`
    AND `the employer is registered for those goods`
